/workspaces/ML-Cancer-Data/openspec/changes/cycle-16-structural-candidate-diversification/proposal.md
diff --git a/openspec/changes/cycle-16-structural-candidate-diversification/proposal.md b/openspec/changes/cycle-16-structural-candidate-diversification/proposal.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7cb45726169b0c95096969a1fca5a89e32a88549
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/cycle-16-structural-candidate-diversification/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+## Why
+
+Hybrid retrieval currently truncates its RRF-ranked union directly to the fixed 20-candidate reranker budget.  Closely related catalog variants can therefore consume most of that budget and hide an otherwise viable variant.  Cycle 13 proposed testing this mechanism but Qdrant was unavailable before evaluation, so it remains a high-information, unevaluated compensation experiment.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add a deterministic pre-rerank diversification stage to the hybrid retrieval path.
+- Build a conservative structural signature from observable catalog evidence only, such as product-family wording, nominal size and pressure, connection, bore/execution, and actuation markers when present.
+- Retain the highest-RRF representative of each reliable signature first, then fill unoccupied reranker slots in existing RRF order with candidates not already retained.
+- Preserve source and alternate retrieval, per-modality de-duplication, RRF scoring, source-query reranking, result format, and fail-open behavior.
+- Add focused tests for duplicate displacement, uncertain/missing catalog fields, rank stability, and matcher integration.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `structural-candidate-diversification`: Produces a bounded, evidence-based diverse candidate pool from hybrid retrieval before LLM reranking.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affected package code: `hybrid_retriever.py`, a small dedicated diversification helper if appropriate, and focused matcher wiring only as needed.
+- Affected tests: hybrid retrieval, matcher, and new diversification unit tests using local fakes/mocks.
+- No catalog data, index representation, embedding model, Qdrant collection, reranker prompt, GOLD/harness artifacts, or index rebuild is required.

