index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..185f2e2c50d4db7dfdf7d659b97e1d2845e34318
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/cycle-16-structural-candidate-diversification/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+## Context
+
+The hybrid retriever obtains up to 50 dense and 50 BM25 results, merges by `ld_id`, applies RRF, sorts the merged union, and immediately slices it to `hybrid_rerank_limit` (20 by default). `NomenclatureMatcher` then sends that list directly to the DeepSeek reranker. See `proposal.md` for motivation and `specs/structural-candidate-diversification/spec.md` for required behavior.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+
+- Make the existing reranker budget cover more reliably distinguishable catalog alternatives.
+- Preserve the exact current result when the source pool has no safe duplicates.
+- Keep the experiment deterministic, local, and independent of Qdrant rebuilds or model calls.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+
+- No eligibility filtering, deterministic product selection, thresholding, or post-rerank override.
+- No inference of unrecorded material, temperature, designation equivalence, flange subtype, or other engineering requirement.
+- No modifications to evaluation/GOLD/harness code, prompts, catalog source, payload schema, or retrieval query generation.
+
+## Decisions
+
+### Diversify after RRF, before the reranker cutoff
+
+Construct the complete already-retrieved RRF-ranked union, derive signatures, choose one representative per safe duplicate group, and only then apply the existing reranker limit. This is the only point that can recover candidates presently lost to the early 20-item slice while retaining the retrieval and scoring system unchanged.
+
+Diversifying each modality before RRF is rejected because it changes fusion evidence. Diversifying after reranking is rejected because it cannot recover omitted candidates and would become a selection intervention.
+
+### Use a conservative evidence-only signature
+
+Create a small pure helper that returns either a signature or no signature. It should normalize only information already carried by `SearchCandidate`: canonicalized product-family cues from name/search text, direct DN/PN/joining fields where available, and exact bounded name/search-text markers for bore/execution and actuation. A candidate with missing, malformed, or ambiguous evidence returns no signature and is never grouped with another candidate merely by partial similarity.
+
+The signature is intentionally not a compatibility schema. Reusing or expanding query constraints is rejected because it would turn a recall-diversification experiment into an eligibility or requirement-extraction experiment, a family that previously regressed or was neutral.
+
+### Deterministic representative and ordering rule
+
+Sort the full union by the current RRF order, breaking exact score ties with a stable deterministic key such as `ld_id`. Traverse this list once: retain the first candidate for each non-null signature and retain every no-signature candidate; then append still-unselected candidates in that same rank order until the configured limit is reached. This makes the highest-ranked duplicate representative win while retaining a predictable, bounded fallback when diverse groups do not fill the budget.
+
+An optimization-style maximal-diversity score is rejected because its weights would be ungrounded and alter rank semantics beyond the stated experiment.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [A too-coarse signature removes a meaningful candidate] → Require all grouping facets to be explicit and treat missing/ambiguous evidence as ungroupable; test close candidates that differ in an observed structural marker.
+- [A too-granular signature yields no diversity benefit] → This is a valid falsifiable outcome; preserve baseline ordering and evaluate through the outer harness.
+- [The full hybrid union exceeds the reranker limit] → Work is bounded by existing dense/BM25 retrieval limits and the existing union; no new requests are made.
+- [Refactoring changes behavior when no duplicates exist] → Add exact regression tests for content and ordering of an all-distinct pool.
+
+## Migration Plan
+
+1. Add the pure, conservative signature and bounded diversification helper with focused unit tests.
+2. Apply it to the already merged and RRF-ranked hybrid union immediately before the existing reranker slice.
+3. Add mocked hybrid-retriever and matcher regression tests; run focused tests and `python -m pytest -q`.
+4. The outer supervisor alone performs public/blind evaluation and promotion or rejection.
+5. Roll back by removing the pre-slice helper call; no persisted data or index migration is involved.
