{"action":"IMPLEMENT","change_name":"cycle-16-structural-candidate-diversification","hypothesis":"Diversifying structurally redundant hybrid candidates before the fixed reranker budget will surface viable variants currently crowded out by near-duplicate catalog entries.","why_now":"Cycle 13 planned this distinct mechanism but Qdrant was unavailable, so it remains unevaluated. It is the best compensation-cycle experiment with credible information gain.","expected_effect":"Retain the highest-RRF representative per reliably evidenced structural signature, then fill remaining reranker capacity in existing RRF order.","expected_metric_gain":"+3.3–6.7 pp hard-pass coverage; no intended safety regression.","lesson_from_history":"Gating, prompts, selection fallbacks, and catalog enrichment were harmful or neutral. Cycles 11–15 were infrastructure-inconclusive; Cycle 13 did not test this hypothesis scientifically.","candidate_hypotheses":["Structural candidate-pool diversification before reranking (selected).","Guarded pipe-OD-to-DN alternate retrieval normalization retry.","Protected-file-safe flange weld-neck subtype verification retry.","Installed-electric versus actuator-ready alternate retrieval expansion retry."],"needs_reindex":false,"plan_summary":"Created and strict-validated proposal, delta spec, design, and implementation-only tasks in openspec/changes/cycle-16-structural-candidate-diversification/. No product code was changed.","used_external_research":false,"research_sources":[],"research_summary":""}
